# deploy-monitor — its OWN environment file (INIT-0038).
#
# Copy to `components/deploy-monitor/.env` on the deploy host. It is loaded by
# docker-compose.yml's `deploy-monitor` service and MUST contain exactly one
# secret and nothing else.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS SEPARATELY FROM components/api/.env:
# `env_file` loads the entire file into the container's environment. Pointing
# this container at the shared api .env would hand the one browser-facing
# process in the stack CAST_JWT_SECRET (HS256 — possession forges any admin
# session), CAST_SECRET_KEY (decrypts every stored integration credential), the
# LDAP bind password, and DEPLOY_AGENT_TOKEN (the full, trigger-capable deploy
# token). That would make the read-only split below decorative — the process
# would hold the trigger credential and merely choose not to use it.
# The security gate BLOCKED exactly that on 2026-08-21. Keep this file minimal.
#
# Add NOTHING else here. If this container ever needs another value, prefer a
# non-secret `environment:` entry in docker-compose.yml over expanding this.

# Read-only credential for deploy-agent. `deploy-agent` accepts this on
# GET /status ONLY and returns 403 for it on every POST route, so the monitor
# can watch a deploy but never start one.
#
# MUST be:
#   - at least 32 characters
#   - DIFFERENT from DEPLOY_AGENT_TOKEN (deploy-agent refuses to start if they
#     match — an identical value would make the split meaningless)
#   - the SAME value as DEPLOY_AGENT_READONLY_TOKEN in components/api/.env,
#     since cast-api uses it as the HMAC key for the watch tokens this
#     container verifies
#
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
DEPLOY_AGENT_READONLY_TOKEN=
